# Shell scripts run inside Linux containers (RabbitMQ init, image builds,
# k8s tooling). A CRLF shebang line fails to exec there — the kernel looks
# for an interpreter literally named "/usr/bin/env bash\r" and gives up with
# exit 127. Windows checkouts with core.autocrlf=true otherwise convert these
# to CRLF on every clone/checkout, which is what broke `pnpm dev`'s
# `rabbitmq-init` step. Force LF regardless of the client's autocrlf setting.
*.sh text eol=lf
